{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes","id":971119,"title":"Which CofD lines work best as standalone universes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-16T20:51:33-07:00","id":971119,"title":"Which CofD lines work best as standalone universes?","content":"With the recent crossover chronicle coming up, I've been wondering about how many people go in the opposite direction: having one line be the focus of the universe, with all or most supernatural phenomena relating only to the systems of that setting. I've been thinking about which lines are the best fit for it. <br /> <br /> Changeling would be my number one pick, just for how broad and flexible and self-contained it is. It would be just as wonderful had it been released as a stand-alone game: it's world is so incredibly rich that it doesn't need anything else. Mage is another good pic, due to the breadth of its setting and its tonal clashes with the rest of the ChroD lines. Genius is another one, since Mane mechanics mean that all supernatural phenomena could easily be explained as Manes. Hunter gets tricky, since the Hunter books themselves leave it ambiguous whether the setting is the wider world of darkness or another setting where the monsters are similar but not quite the same. Promethean and Mummy would require major expansion to fully hold up a supernatural ecosystem. <br /> <br /> I've actually always imagined ChroD and WoD existing as a massive network of parallel universes, each representing a different edition, iteration, or version of the setting. So, there's a world where Genius is canon, and all supernatural phenomena come from Mania. There's one where only Leviathan and Mummy are canon. There's one where the Technocracy fights the Seers over a post-apocalyptic hellscape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:13:12-07:00","id":971131,"title":"","content":"Demon's Storyteller Guide provides a version of that I believe, through the speculations of Demons on what other things might be in relation to the God-Machine. All you gotta do is decide they're right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:16:43-07:00","id":971158,"title":"","content":"Mummy and Demon make the best little pocket universes, I think. Mummy basically acts like the most important things in the world are the works of Irem and the will of the Judges and the Devourer, while Demon works incredibly well as &quot;all of the weird shit is enemy action from the Machine.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:53:24-07:00","id":971173,"title":"","content":"Beast, beast is definitely the most self-contained game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T22:59:13-07:00","id":971174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971158#post971158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mummy and Demon make the best little pocket universes, I think. Mummy basically acts like the most important things in the world are the works of Irem and the will of the Judges and the Devourer, while Demon works incredibly well as &quot;all of the weird shit is enemy action from the Machine.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>While it can work that way, I personally find Demon works even better as part of a larger setting. Demons -think- that everything's caused by the God-Machine, but in reality it's only one piece of a much larger puzzle and their paranoia has lead them away from truth.<br /> Mummy does seem like that sometimes to me, though.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think Mage also has enough to support itself as a standalone setting. Though I feel it is only improved with crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T23:28:36-07:00","id":971179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971174#post971174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it can work that way, I personally find Demon works even better as part of a larger setting. Demons -think- that everything's caused by the God-Machine, but in reality it's only one piece of a much larger puzzle and their paranoia has lead them away from truth.<br /> Mummy does seem like that sometimes to me, though.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think Mage also has enough to support itself as a standalone setting. Though I feel it is only improved with crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue Mage is the best gameline for crossover, even over Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T03:57:53-07:00","id":971239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971179#post971179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd argue Mage is the best gameline for crossover, even over Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's great for crossover, but at the same time it's a great game to totally ignore the other splats with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:11:21-07:00","id":971261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971239#post971239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's great for crossover, but at the same time it's a great game to totally ignore the other splats with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is <i>definition</i> of 'game great as standalone universe'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So <b>Mage</b> is also my own voice on topics question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:30:11-07:00","id":971294,"title":"","content":"All of them except Beast and Hunter. Self contained game is the default, even in Mage. Crossover is such a big thing right now because its a variation from the norm. But each game is designed to shine the best when run by their own.<br /> <br /> Beast and Hunter are the exceptiosn because those two games are designed to go around and interact / hunt other supernaturals. In fact, I argue that, without other supernaturals, there is no Beast / Hunter games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-17-2016, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:34:06-07:00","id":971388,"title":"","content":"I believe Mage, Changeling, Promethean, Geist and Mummy work best as standalone universes. Their focuses are mostly internal and nothing is really gained by bringing in other lines. While I can understand people thinking Mage is good for crossover, it certainly has enough Mysteries in it as is, and if you've seen any of the cosmology threads you've likely seen everything else being dismissed as some spawn of the 'Lower Depths,' and dismissed. Anyone who's read Dave Brookshaw's Actual Plays would notice the game didn't really gain anything by the presence of the wolf-blooded, and arguably his games have inspired a lot of the second edition setting. That said, I haven't gotten through the Man in Black so feel free to point out if there's any other supernaturals there. Changeling and Promethean both have parts of the game that encourage them to interact with other supernatural lines, but again I don't think it brings anything to their table, I don't believe anyone off-hand except perhaps the Free Council would offer something to Promethean. Geist and Mummy are drastically different from other games, and like Changeling and Promethean really have an internal focus that just sort of gets muddied down by other lines.<br /> <br /> On the other side of the coin, I think Werewolf, Hunter, Demon and Beast work really well as crossover universes. Both Werewolf and Hunter are brought other antagonists, and while you can have them as Horrors or other beings, I think the hunt in both games get more depth when you have the full lines backing those antagonists. A lone vampire is good for a couple sessions, bring an entire society and their covenants into the picture and you have a much more in-depth story. I think the only problem with Beast being crossover is that they are more in-line and likely to ally with the traditional antagonists of other lines, and I believe the people who've proclaimed they like Beast have also shown that they don't like those antagonists.<br /> <br /> Vampire I think is probably the best borderline game that can go either way. If you want to focus on the All Night's Society, and politics and the 'family,' using just Vampire is more than enough. But bringing in the other lines to bump heads with the 'rulers' of the night can add an element of tense fragility to their nature of superiority, and when Vampires can find allies with the other supernaturals, they are capable of bringing strange and deadly weapons and loves to it.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Deviant being crossover friendly, but obviously it's too early to say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:38:19-07:00","id":971393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971173#post971173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast, beast is definitely the most self-contained game.</div> </div> </div> </div>All lies, total lies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:52:19-07:00","id":971403,"title":"","content":"In order of best to worst for single line, none crossover universes Mummy, Promeathan, Changeling, Demon, Vampire, Werewolf, Sin Eaters, Mage, and lastly Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:26:15-07:00","id":971455,"title":"","content":"IMO, Hunter actually works really well as its own self-contained universe. It already breaks the rules of the other gamelines pretty regularly, and you don't need Vampires, Werewolves or Mages to have vampires, werewolves or mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:51:11-07:00","id":971472,"title":"","content":"I think Mummy was even written to be a standalone universe.<br /> <br /> I guess it depends on exactly what you mean because vampires exist in all the lines, but Vampires only exist in one. There is no rule preventing anyone from bringing Vampires into any other line but that is not the default scenario. Hybrid games exist, more than one game line present. Beast is a hybrid game by default, but there still is no requirement of Vampires over vampires. So far, Beast is the only default hybrid game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:51:00-07:00","id":971652,"title":"","content":"I admit, my calling Mage better as a standalone is mostly due to tonal dissatisfaction. <br /> <br /> And Deviant is shaping up to be very crossover-friendly. In fact, since it doesn't specify the source of Deviant powers (which could be any number of things), it sort of assumes that other supernatural forces already exist in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:54:09-07:00","id":971655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971472#post971472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mummy was even written to be a standalone universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't written to be standalone, but it sure as hell was designed to be stand alone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:01:11-07:00","id":971732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971655#post971655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't written to be standalone, but it sure as hell was designed to be stand alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about the distinction. IIRC the developer actually would just assume the other lines not exist in Mummy. I was referring to that. Seems to me like they ended up with leaving the door open but your on your own making it fit through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T21:08:49-07:00","id":971738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971732#post971732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure about the distinction. IIRC the developer actually would just assume the other lines not exist in Mummy. I was referring to that. Seems to me like they ended up with leaving the door open but your on your own making it fit through.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was mostly just saying &quot;Yeah, you're right&quot; with some light elaboration. It's not really my place to talk about it since I wasn't involved, though, so that's about all you get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:13:15-07:00","id":971785,"title":"","content":"I'm sticking with Mage as being good for a standalone, because I honestly think it needs a lot of work to crossover well, or else it becomes &quot;too-cool superheroes helping out suckers who weren't as lucky as they were&quot;. Like, imagine you're a Changeling, and some smug Dr. Who knockoff (the Acanthus Free Council Gary Stu everyone has) shows up and starts lecturing you, basically about how he has vastly greater powers than you do but he had to suffer infinitely less for them. It's pretty damn hard to do without shitting on the other games.<br /> <br /> I feel like splitting the two does wonders for both of them. Putting Mage in its own World of Dark Superhero The Matrix Adventures lets it shine, and excising it from ChroD while leaving the rest in (and having magic users exclusively be sorcerers and hedge wizards) just fits the setting so much better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-18-2016, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:42:38-07:00","id":971795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971785#post971785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, imagine you're a Changeling, and some smug Dr. Who knockoff (the Acanthus Free Council Gary Stu everyone has) shows up and starts lecturing you, basically about how he has vastly greater powers than you do but he had to suffer infinitely less for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because, as we all know, supernatural beings are chiefly concerned with one-upsmanship re: their superpowers.<br /> <br /> Changelings are going to run into problems with mages principally on the same basis as demons would \u2014 a lot of potentially-invasive scrutiny putting your well-being in the hands of strangers \u2014 or as they would with Beasts \u2014 the other guy's magical nature has a significant incentive to probe at the boundaries of your comfort zone for reasons that boil down to &quot;to see what happens.&quot; That the mage might be far-gone enough that they aren't bothering with a nonmagical identity and are massively fronting about what their Awakening meant has little to no bearing on how one of the Lost feels about their powers not being as elemental as wizard-magic.<br /> <br /> The expectation that players will not create obviously terrible characters does not have an exception clause of &quot;unless you're running a mage in a crossover game.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:46:13-07:00","id":971796,"title":"","content":"I mean, I guess I kind of have a bigger complaint here, in that the whole issue of the most human and least monstrous splat being the most powerful always bothered me a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-18-2016, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T01:14:15-07:00","id":971819,"title":"","content":"So we say standalone do we mean without crossovers in player land or NPC land? I think any of them work fine without crossovers in player land, but I like to bring in other splats, and other splats antagonists into NPC land.<br /> <br /> Though if I had to wager a guess, perhaps the most interesting to not bring other splats in as NPCs is Promethean. Prometheans don't need vampires or mages to be foils they're trying to become human, and humanity is perhaps their biggest foil as well as themselves.<br /> <br /> That said I've never actually run Promethean, I thought they made better NPCs in 1e. I might with 2e now that rules regarding disquiet, wasteland and throngs are better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 09-18-2016, 04:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T06:00:57-07:00","id":971897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971785#post971785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sticking with Mage as being good for a standalone, because I honestly think it needs a lot of work to crossover well, or else it becomes &amp;quot;too-cool superheroes helping out suckers who weren't as lucky as they were&amp;quot;. Like, imagine you're a Changeling, and some smug Dr. Who knockoff (the Acanthus Free Council Gary Stu everyone has) shows up and starts lecturing you, basically about how he has vastly greater powers than you do but he had to suffer infinitely less for them. It's pretty damn hard to do without shitting on the other games.<br /> <br /> I feel like splitting the two does wonders for both of them. Putting Mage in its own World of Dark Superhero The Matrix Adventures lets it shine, and excising it from ChroD while leaving the rest in (and having magic users exclusively be sorcerers and hedge wizards) just fits the setting so much better.</div> </div> </div> </div> That mage would like come to regret that arrogance when the Changeling dumps him somewhere in the Hedge with no way back out.<br /> <br /> Or if the Changeling can just point out the longer natural lifespan then the Mage, or Seal one of the Athacus stupid statements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:23:26-07:00","id":971936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971785#post971785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sticking with Mage as being good for a standalone, because I honestly think it needs a lot of work to crossover well, or else it becomes &quot;too-cool superheroes helping out suckers who weren't as lucky as they were&quot;. Like, imagine you're a Changeling, and some smug Dr. Who knockoff (the Acanthus Free Council Gary Stu everyone has) shows up and starts lecturing you, basically about how he has vastly greater powers than you do but he had to suffer infinitely less for them. It's pretty damn hard to do without shitting on the other games.<br /> <br /> I feel like splitting the two does wonders for both of them. Putting Mage in its own World of Dark Superhero The Matrix Adventures lets it shine, and excising it from ChroD while leaving the rest in (and having magic users exclusively be sorcerers and hedge wizards) just fits the setting so much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a Mage problem, this is a Bad Mage Fan problem. There have been tons of threads over the years where people have reported putting mages into crossovers and had it work out fine, particularly the more a given ST knew how to work with the dynamics.<br /> <br /> It seems easy to suggest that mages are so overpowered compared to other splats, but considering I have personally done some mage asskickings with a few changelings in my time of playing the game, I will tell you here and now that it's not the characters, it's the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T09:32:52-07:00","id":971971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971936#post971936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not a Mage problem, this is a Bad Mage Fan problem. There have been tons of threads over the years where people have reported putting mages into crossovers and had it work out fine, particularly the more a given ST knew how to work with the dynamics.<br /> <br /> It seems easy to suggest that mages are so overpowered compared to other splats, but considering I have personally done some mage asskickings with a few changelings in my time of playing the game, I will tell you here and now that it's not the characters, it's the players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it's also possible that it's a rules confusion problem... in changeling 1 I was very confused about how their powers worked... and they read a lot more nerfed and useless than they were (I thought they could only be used under special condition). So it might have been how it was written... That said I suspect an Arisen or a Demon could also take on a Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:26:30-07:00","id":971995,"title":"","content":"A 2e Changeling could take on a mage, especially if they have a high wyrd and high clarity. At high clarity Changelings can be highly resistant to mind control and perception distorting magics. At high wyrd Embracing the Wyrd becomes extremely powerful verstile. A Wyrd 10/ Clarity 10 Changeling will crush most none Archmage mages. At Wyrd 10 embracing the wyrd gives a Changeling a bonus dice pool of 10 per turn +1 extra die per Glamour spent, which at wyrd 10 is, 15 Glamour per turn. And that's before factoring other possible boons like a, Goblin Vow giving them a +3 dice on all rolls.<br /> <br /> And that's just the type of the iceberg. At lower wyrd the key trick is Dropping the Mask, which has a variety of benifits which includes exceptional success on certain contracts and auto successes on contract where the amount of successes matters. Actually a high wyrd changeling benfits from this too, getting either an automatic exceptional success or 10 free successes is nothing to snear at.<br /> <br /> A High Wyrd changeling can basically be awesome at anything, if its willing to take the risk/pay the price.<br /> <br /> A Vampire Elder is nothing to snear at either, even for a mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T12:15:48-07:00","id":972062,"title":"","content":"If you want to maintain a world which has myths about all of the various creatures, Changeling or Mage are the obvious choices since either of them could be the basis of all other monster myths. Changeling is probably the easiest, since the various seemings and kiths of Changelings pretty much cover the entire spectrum of other monsters including vampires (Darkling Leechfinger), ghosts (Darkling Palewraith), zombies and mummies (Darkling Gravewright), prometheans (Elemental Mannikin), demons (Fairest Draconic, among others), mages (various Wizened and Darkling kiths), werewolves (Beast Hunterheart), and even mad scientists (Wizened Inventor). Mages, on the other hand, could similarly use Life to produce effects that were the origins of werewolf myths, Death to produce effects that originated vampire myths, etc. <br /> <br /> I'd also add Demon, given the variety of Demonic Forms and cryptids.<br /> <br /> It would be difficult to say the same for Vampire, Werewolf, or most of the other lines. It could be done (such as saying Gangrel were the source of werewolf myths), but some things would be a bit of a stretch (such as Vampires being the source of any sort of creature myth related to or seen during the day, or Mummies or Prometheans being the source of a great many other creature myths).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12354-who-is-matt","name":"who.is.matt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:34:13-07:00","id":972130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fumus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971173#post971173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast, beast is definitely the most self-contained game.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is sort of strange that they made Beast the Primordial THE crossover game. To me it doesn't seem to mix well with the others, even with itself it feels like the beast were originally intended to be lone wolf characters, rather than broods.<br /> <br /> As for the best games for their own self contained universe, I would put Demon, and Mage together with the God Machine Chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:29:48-07:00","id":972168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972130#post972130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is sort of strange that they made Beast the Primordial THE crossover game. To me it doesn't seem to mix well with the others, even with itself it feels like the beast were originally intended to be lone wolf characters, rather than broods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like with Werewolf and Demon, Beast takes the tack that the more infamous and legendary examples are simply the ones that most frequently catch press. Beasts who trend toward Kinship over Hunger tend to focus more on blending in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:31:37-07:00","id":972170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=971738#post971738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was mostly just saying &quot;Yeah, you're right&quot; with some light elaboration. It's not really my place to talk about it since I wasn't involved, though, so that's about all you get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. I didn't get that so I was confused. I wasn't involved either so I was trying to do the same. Carry on. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:41:27-07:00","id":972176,"title":"","content":"I'ma be blunt: I don't understand this idea that Beast somehow failed in being the crossover game. Some of y'all saying that, unpack it for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:08:08-07:00","id":972271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972176#post972176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'ma be blunt: I don't understand this idea that Beast somehow failed in being the crossover game. Some of y'all saying that, unpack it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't answer for the others, but for me it seems that the only Crossover that's backed up mechanically in Beast is Kinship and Family dinner, which seem a bit vague and tacked on. As in, you could easily drop them and not lose anything or even strengthen Beast's... themes? Mood? &lt;shrug&gt;<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is, while Beast talks much about family and such, it feels very forced. But, again, that's just my take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:11:35-07:00","id":972273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972176#post972176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'ma be blunt: I don't understand this idea that Beast somehow failed in being the crossover game. Some of y'all saying that, unpack it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already stated otherwise, but I think I can see where some of them are coming from.<br /> <br /> There's little incentive to bring a Beast into a game full of other supernaturals over, say, any other supernatural. Just looking at some of the fiction, for instance, in three of the stories I read that had Beasts involved with other supernaturals, it was because they were friends. Not out of any specific Beast-hood. You could have put a Demon or a Mage or a Werewolf in their place and not missed a stride.<br /> <br /> The fact that Beasts are aligned more often with the 'antagonist' groups should disincline most y-splats with interacting with them.<br /> <br /> Presumably there's more, this is just what I see and I think it's alright for crossover.<br /> <br /> How about you suggest reasons why you believe Beast succeeded in being a crossover game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:16:25-07:00","id":972279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972273#post972273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've already stated otherwise, but I think I can see where some of them are coming from.<br /> <br /> There's little incentive to bring a Beast into a game full of other supernaturals over, say, any other supernatural. Just looking at some of the fiction, for instance, in three of the stories I read that had Beasts involved with other supernaturals, it was because they were friends. Not out of any specific Beast-hood. You could have put a Demon or a Mage or a Werewolf in their place and not missed a stride.<br /> <br /> The fact that Beasts are aligned more often with the 'antagonist' groups should disincline most y-splats with interacting with them.<br /> <br /> Presumably there's more, this is just what I see and I think it's alright for crossover.<br /> <br /> How about you suggest reasons why you believe Beast succeeded in being a crossover game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need some perspective on the matter first, and that asides, it fits with the conversation of Stand-Alone Universes better if I let the conversation go in that direction for a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T05:34:39-07:00","id":972460,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don\u2018t think Beasts are crossover unfriendly, but I do think if you were to give out points to the different splats based on how crossover friendly they are Beasts would get less than most other splats. IMO The only ones that might get less points are Prometheans, Mummies, and possibly Demons.<br /> <br /> Powerwise, Beasts don't really have anything special to offer for crossover games. Sure, they get ways to buff others, but every single splat get those and Beasts aren't exceptionally better at it. Those few extra dice they can give though the Kinship Link aren\u2018t exactly mind blowing, and are easily matched by buffs most other splats have to offer.<br /> <br /> Themes-wise, they lack mechanical support for one thing that most other splats that I consider more crossover friendly share, which is the fight to stay ethical/human/balanced. There are differences there, but even werewolves need to think about their actions, and it creates a connection between Werewolves, Mages, Hunters, Changelings, possibly Sin-Eaters, and even Vampires. Sure, a Beast PC can decide to care about these things, but it's left wholly to the player with zero mechanical incentives behind it.<br /> <br /> On the social side, Beasts are limited to being either solo or part of a very small scale group \u2013 their brood. So while most other splats allow for political intrigues, divided loyalties, variable scale political manoeuvring and access to completely new resources as characters that are part of several different social networks suddenly come into contact, Beasts have far less to offer for crossovers in this. Getting a Mage into your crossover chronicle also brings the story potential from their membership in their Cabal, their Order, their Legacy, their Consilium, and their relationship to their their Mentor(s), all of which can be used for great potential story effect. Beasts only ever bring their Brood and possibly their Devourer, at most.<br /> <br /> Motivationally, family Dinner and Kinship give the Beast a reason to work with others splats, but only the Beast really gets anything out of it. I also think Family Dinner isn't as special at creating a motivation to work with other splats as it's made out to be. Most splats get plenty of inherent motivation to work with others. Mages have their Obsessions and curiosity, Changelings and Werewolves have antagonists that are powerful enough that they are motivated to take every help they can get their hands on, in their games of courtly intrigue Vampires want every ace up their sleeve they can get their cold dead hands on, Mummies are on the lookout for every new resource that can help them locate and get their hands on relics, and Prometheans can even get Milestones out of interacting with other monsters. Beasts lack basically all of these reasons with the possible exception of having allies that have an easier time dealing with Heroes, which makes Family Dinner feel more like a band aid to make up for lacking any crossover motivation that grew naturally from their situation and mindset.<br /> <br /> On a note of personal annoyance, I hate that Beasts have all these coherent ideas about their history and purpose, yet zero explanation as to why these theories are so unanimously known. Ideas like \u201ewe are all part of a family\u201c or \u201eBeasts exist to teach lessons\u201c seem to be created from nothing in their minds at the moment of devouring. Why does an individual Beast believe other monsters are family, who told them? Most other splats have explanations for why certain facts are widely known like Changelings being members of a Court that shares and keeps knowledge. Beast doesn\u2018t, and when a Beast joins a chronicle the ST has to find the explanation themselves. Did their Devourer teach them? Then who told the Devourer? What if the Beast self-devoured? Who made sure that both the newly born Beast in Africa and the old Dragon in the Antarctic know that Beasts should teach lessons? It\u2018s extra work for the ST, and personally I definitely remove a few points of crossover friendliness from them for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 09-19-2016, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:09:44-07:00","id":972473,"title":"","content":"I'd say Mummy is the most stand alone because all other beginning Characters start with 1 or if they sacrifice merit dots, 2 or 3 in their power stat, a Mummy starts with 10 in their power stat and get weaker as the others get stronger.<br /> <br /> Its like the Mummy us starting at Finish Line and racing back towards the Starting Line, while everyone else starts at the Starting Line and ends at the Finishing Line. They just not crossover compatible at all, it was my big complaint about Mummy and why even though I backed its kickstarter, I have the least interest in it of all game lines. Its just does things backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:21:52-07:00","id":972476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972176#post972176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'ma be blunt: I don't understand this idea that Beast somehow failed in being the crossover game. Some of y'all saying that, unpack it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think its because people focus so much on feeding Hungers and Atavisms (admittedly the sexist of the Beast powers) that they completely miss the other parts of the game. A lot of people, when they come to Beast to play the game, want to feel like they're actuall Medusa, or a dragon, or a giant. You get that mostly from Hunger and Low Satiety Atavisms. So, it naturally gets the most focus when people read it, and the other things &quot;feel tacked on&quot; because they're not what people are looking for.<br /> <br /> Then, I think people are also thinking about bringing Beasts into other games. What does having a Beast in a Vampire game offer? A Mage game? I get the impression that, rather than Beasts having crossover as the focus of a BtP game, people expect Beasts to be easily inserted into another gameline. People want there to be a reason for another supernatural to care about the Beast beyond Social Maneuvering, friendship, Mother's Kiss and the advantages of numbers. The questions seem to be &quot;Why should my changeling care about a Beast?&quot; rather than &quot;why should my Beast care about other supernaturals?&quot; Its a question of outsiders looking at a Beast and wondering what's in it for them. <br /> <br /> I think that there's some expectations here that the game isn't designed to address - Beast is designed to give the Begotten reasons to interact with others, but it is not designed to give others a reason to interact and be friends with Beasts. I get the feeling that people want more mechanical incentives for other supers to be friends with the Beast to the point it would be dumb to not be friends. Granted, that also goes against the theme of Beast - crossover doesn't mean you are always friends. In fact, you are just as often antagonists towards supernaturals, falling into dividing lines and the like. Hells, you even make other supernaturals you're enemies with into Kin and feed off them! But the expectation seems to be still &quot;must be friends.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972271#post972271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't answer for the others, but for me it seems that the only Crossover that's backed up mechanically in Beast is Kinship and Family dinner, which seem a bit vague and tacked on. As in, you could easily drop them and not lose anything or even strengthen Beast's... themes? Mood? &lt;shrug&gt;</div> </div> </div> </div>* Nightmares grow from interacting with non-Beasts<br /> * Lairs grow from hearing stories from other supernaturals<br /> * Family Dinner allows you to maintain high Satiety easily, whereas its nearly impossible with Hunger<br /> * Mother's Blessing is a thing<br /> * Ability to enter any supernatural world alongside others so you won't get left behind when someone goes visiting the Hisil or Hedge<br /> * Ability to instantly recognize other supernaturals on sight, even through concealment effects<br /> * Ability to establish Kinship easily through Social Maneuvering in various ways. Nightmares are literally designed for this via Forcing Doors / Hard Leverage.<br /> * Low-level mind control to make other supernaturals not instantly flip out over being exposed as a supernatural and feel at ease.<br /> <br /> The mechanics to back this theme up are everywhere. Not always obvious, but absolutely there. So, the question becomes.... why do people downplay these parts? Just not realize it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-19-2016, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:33:11-07:00","id":972482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972476#post972476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mechanics to back this theme up are everywhere. Not always obvious, but absolutely there. So, the question becomes.... why do people downplay these parts?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely award beasts crossover points for all the things you listed, but I disagree with them being all that special and more influential among all the other crossover enabling powers and motivation-providers you find in other splats.<br /> You say they get downplayed, I say they get overplayed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T06:51:39-07:00","id":972490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972476#post972476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hells, you even make other supernaturals you're enemies with into Kin and feed off them! But the expectation seems to be still &quot;must be friends.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> * Nightmares grow from interacting with non-Beasts<br /> * Lairs grow from hearing stories from other supernaturals<br /> * Family Dinner allows you to maintain high Satiety easily, whereas its nearly impossible with Hunger<br /> * Mother's Blessing is a thing<br /> * Ability to enter any supernatural world alongside others so you won't get left behind when someone goes visiting the Hisil or Hedge<br /> * Ability to instantly recognize other supernaturals on sight, even through concealment effects<br /> * Ability to establish Kinship easily through Social Maneuvering in various ways. Nightmares are literally designed for this via Forcing Doors / Hard Leverage.<br /> * Low-level mind control to make other supernaturals not instantly flip out over being exposed as a supernatural and feel at ease.<br /> <br /> The mechanics to back this theme up are everywhere. Not always obvious, but absolutely there. So, the question becomes.... why do people downplay these parts? Just not realize it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The writing, I certainly didn't realize half the things you just said, and in fact some of them I wouldn't mind citations. I also think beast is so new... it needs at least one more book before people will really grok it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:06:41-07:00","id":972496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972476#post972476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* Nightmares grow from interacting with non-Beasts<br /> * Lairs grow from hearing stories from other supernaturals<br /> * Family Dinner allows you to maintain high Satiety easily, whereas its nearly impossible with Hunger<br /> * Mother's Blessing is a thing<br /> * Ability to enter any supernatural world alongside others so you won't get left behind when someone goes visiting the Hisil or Hedge<br /> * Ability to instantly recognize other supernaturals on sight, even through concealment effects<br /> * Ability to establish Kinship easily through Social Maneuvering in various ways. Nightmares are literally designed for this via Forcing Doors / Hard Leverage.<br /> * Low-level mind control to make other supernaturals not instantly flip out over being exposed as a supernatural and feel at ease.</div> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>They don't need to. You can form Nightmares without ever encountering another Supernatural.</li> <li>They don't need to, and it doesn't even seem to be the primary means of growth.</li> <li>Family dinner, as I said, seems tacked on to me. It seems to reduce the themes of feeding and monstrous-ness when all you might need to do is play voyeur.</li> <li>Mother's Kiss is a generic Dice Bonus. Mage's Fate Arcana can do similar (if not the same).</li> <li>Skeleton Key seems tacked on.</li> <li>Recognition seems tacked on.</li> </ul>Basically, Kinship feels tacked on. You could drop it and lose nothing about a game of monsters and fears. You could add it to any other splat and it would fit almost as well. It just doesn't seem all that integrated into <i>Beast</i>, just something that was &quot;well, it needs to be the crossover game, so let's just force some stuff in there.&quot; To me, at least.<br /> <br /> Now, I get <i>why</i> that is likely the case: you can't <i>mandate</i> crossover (and require people to buy more books), so it itself needs to be optional and not delve too deeply into any one specific. But some of the &quot;Cross-over powers&quot; could have tied into Beast's Fear themes a bit better (Recognition could pick up the distinct aura and nature of fear about a Werewolf/Vampire/Mage, etc. instead of just &quot;Yep, that's a Changeling alright&quot;, Skeleton Key doesn't seem needed - if the Splat has a way into Otherworld X, they usually also have some way of bringing people with, or you could base a custom Nightmare around it.). I get why &quot;we're all related&quot; seems new and forced - it has to be generic, and Beast is a new line, so of course the concept is also going to be new (since they couldn't have very well implemented suggestions prior to this existing... or could they?).<br /> <br /> Yes, there is material there. It just feels forced in. And yes, I understand likely why. But that's still how it feels to me.<br /> <br /> Hunter seems more integrated with Crossover (in theme, if not mechanics), because without other monsters, what do Hunters hunt? It's core to their very concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:43:13-07:00","id":972519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972496#post972496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>They don't need to. You can form Nightmares without ever encountering another Supernatural.</li> <li>They don't need to, and it doesn't even seem to be the primary means of growth.</li> <li>Family dinner, as I said, seems tacked on to me. It seems to reduce the themes of feeding and monstrous-ness when all you might need to do is play voyeur.</li> <li>Mother's Kiss is a generic Dice Bonus. Mage's Fate Arcana can do similar (if not the same).</li> <li>Skeleton Key seems tacked on.</li> <li>Recognition seems tacked on.</li> </ul>Basically, Kinship feels tacked on.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Feels tacked on&quot; is not an explanation; you're dismissing large parts of the game just because you don't like them. Irregardless if something feels &quot;forced&quot; or you want it stronger or whatever? The fact remains that its an innate ability of every Beast and there's the drive to do these things through the carrot method. And you cannot deny the sheer weight of things.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't understand why people feel there needs to be an suppeen contest. Who cares what a mage can do*? It doesn't change the drives or abilities of the Beasts. Makes me think that the real explanation is &quot;I'd just rather play another game and build for crossover.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Hunter seems more integrated with Crossover (in theme, if not mechanics), because without other monsters, what do Hunters hunt? It's core to their very concept.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> Hunters can't go running through the Hisil with werewolves to hunt down a spirit for essence. Beasts do it as a matter of course. While still crossover, its a completely different kind of crossover that defaults to antagonistic. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T07:45:37-07:00","id":972522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972490#post972490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The writing, I certainly didn't realize half the things you just said, and in fact some of them I wouldn't mind citations. I also think beast is so new... it needs at least one more book before people will really grok it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure? Which ones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T10:04:02-07:00","id":972580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972519#post972519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Feels tacked on&quot; is not an explanation;</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;ex\u00b7pla\u00b7na\u00b7tion: </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">a reason or justification given for an action or belief.&quot; I literally gave you my reasons for it feeling tacked on. You may not <i>like</i> them, or agree with them, but that doesn't change the fact that they exist.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972519#post972519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you're dismissing large parts of the game just because you don't like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'm saying I feel like they were added solely for &quot;Crossover&quot; rather than arising from the concept of Beasts and those joined with a Primordial Fear-thing. I don't &quot;like&quot; the attempts at abuse justification, but I'm not dismissing those.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972519#post972519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irregardless if something feels &quot;forced&quot; or you want it stronger or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a question or a statement?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972519#post972519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact remains that its an innate ability of every Beast and there's the drive to do these things through the carrot method.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of which prevents it from feeling tacked on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972519#post972519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you cannot deny the sheer weight of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not denying them - I'm saying they feel forced to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972519#post972519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't understand why people feel there needs to be an suppeen contest. Who cares what a mage can do*? It doesn't change the drives or abilities of the Beasts. Makes me think that the real explanation is &quot;I'd just rather play another game and build for crossover.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an example of how their &quot;crossover ability&quot; (well, one of them) is hardly unique or interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972519#post972519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters can't go running through the Hisil with werewolves to hunt down a spirit for essence. Beasts do it as a matter of course. While still crossover, its a completely different kind of crossover that defaults to antagonistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure they can - they just need to be brought with via a Rite, or find a Locus/Verge. And sure, it is usually antagonistic... but &quot;Cancer Cells&quot; do exist as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:32:58-07:00","id":972724,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm gonna say that while Beast definitely could have been better and I have gripes with it, I'm with arc in that the crossover element never struck me as being particularly weak. I thought it worked well, but the problem was that people who didn't like Beast for other reasons objected to it, because it felt to them like they were being pushed to include Beasts in their games. That's kind of why Mage getting a crossover focus irks me a bit too.<br /> <br /> As for Mage, I've moving towards splitting it in a different way: Mage as written takes place in The World of Dark Occult Superheroes, while in the main ChroD the Awakened are the rare, broken, volatile result of a sorcerer or hedge mage going way too deep into the fabric of reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:41:47-07:00","id":972737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972473#post972473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Mummy is the most stand alone because all other beginning Characters start with 1 or if they sacrifice merit dots, 2 or 3 in their power stat, a Mummy starts with 10 in their power stat and get weaker as the others get stronger.<br /> <br /> Its like the Mummy us starting at Finish Line and racing back towards the Starting Line, while everyone else starts at the Starting Line and ends at the Finishing Line. They just not crossover compatible at all, it was my big complaint about Mummy and why even though I backed its kickstarter, I have the least interest in it of all game lines. Its just does things backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>As has been said about a lot of things, feature, not bug. I'd have complained about that when I supported the kickstarter but I was never promised a game that was going to be deeply set as a crossover setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-19-2016, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T15:13:16-07:00","id":972759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972724#post972724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mage, I've moving towards splitting it in a different way: Mage as written takes place in The World of Dark Occult Superheroes, while in the main ChroD the Awakened are the rare, broken, volatile result of a sorcerer or hedge mage going way too deep into the fabric of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your continuing to assert this does not make it true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T16:06:35-07:00","id":972799,"title":"","content":"He means the problem is people run stories where they're dark superheroes because they're missing the point. To be fair many people play Vampire the same way (Dark Sexy Superheroes) (and 1e werewolf basically had it written in). I think when you're ... arrogant ... and know just enough to be dangerous... that often you are not aware of that. I think that many people are playing mage exactly as they'd want to be but because hubris is often blind to the fact, they are too. To be fair superheroes themselves (on that note Dr Strange looks awesome) frequently have victims their hubris (Ultron?), so in some ways perhaps the comparison isn't unfair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 09-19-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:24:13-07:00","id":972835,"title":"","content":"No, I think Dave has the right of it and the person he's quoting is a member of that fraternity who want Mage to be a palette swap of other gamelines so it can meet some arbitrary standard of YOU MUST BE THIS HORROR TO RIDE THIS RIDE.<br /> <br /> And I don't think people who don't play it that way are &quot;missing the point.&quot; I think there's a vast excluded middle between Korn album and &quot;lol superheroes lol&quot; and the people playing in that middle have read the fiction and rules and interpreted them just fine.<br /> <br /> And even if they were missing the point - so what? One-true-wayism is a disease of the mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T17:35:41-07:00","id":972838,"title":"","content":"As for the thread topic, I vacillate. I feel like every ChronD game can generally coexist reasonably well with the others, especially if used sparingly to spice up your currently-being-played game with hints of a wider world, but I also feel like a lot of needless complexity is avoided if you run the other monsters/splats as more archetypal versions of themselves. If I'm running Hunter and there's a vampire in the story, I'm just as likely to make him a random vampire bro with fangs and a cape and a dodgy accent than to make him a Kindred\u2122 of the Gangrel\u2122 clan. If you want to use a mummy as a generic monster, there's nothing wrong with having him leap out of the tomb going BOOGITY BOOGITY BOO instead of painstakingly describing his Judge and figuring out his Sekhem and et cetera et cetera.<br /> <br /> All that said, I think Mage and Hunter are probably most dependent on the presence of other gamelines - it would be weird if Hunters had nothing to hunt, after all, and it would be almost as weird if Mages existed in a world of limitless magical possibilities -except- for vampires and werewolves and Frankensteins - and I think the games that can stand most independently are probably Demon and Vampire. Vampire because it was the first and prototypical urban horror fiction and doesn't automatically suggest the existence of other supernaturals, and Demon because it is so utterly sui generis and comes complete with an internally-consistent cosmology that explains everything Demons are and can encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T20:36:35-07:00","id":972907,"title":"","content":"Eh. It's an opinion matter. I like a lot about Mage, it just takes a bit to get it to work with my vision of ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T02:42:32-07:00","id":973007,"title":"","content":"Mummy largely has to stand alone, in its current form its not crossover viable, so that makes it the winner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T03:50:48-07:00","id":973025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972473#post972473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Mummy is the most stand alone because all other beginning Characters start with 1 or if they sacrifice merit dots, 2 or 3 in their power stat, a Mummy starts with 10 in their power stat and get weaker as the others get stronger.<br /> <br /> Its like the Mummy us starting at Finish Line and racing back towards the Starting Line, while everyone else starts at the Starting Line and ends at the Finishing Line. They just not crossover compatible at all, it was my big complaint about Mummy and why even though I backed its kickstarter, I have the least interest in it of all game lines. Its just does things backwards.</div> </div> </div> </div>During Sothic Turns Mummies don't lose their last dot of Sekhem through passing time. So I always wanted to to play a mummy in a crossover game that started the game deep enough into a Turn to be at Sekhem 1. The risk of getting back into that whole cycle of rebirth, memory loss, and servitude would give you more than enough motivation to try and stay alive, and the ST could even rule that if it happens you have to make a different character. Instead of increasing your power stat with xp its advancement would happen through buying powers and 'finding' Talismans, both of which can provide virtual increases to Sekhem under specific circumstances (like that one power that makes your Sekhem count as five dots higher while inside your tomb).<br /> Ideally, the game would start without any player knowing what splats each other's character belongs to.<br /> <br /> Could be fun. Add a Cult based around secrecy and make the Mummy motivated enough to increase Memory that it <i>really</i> doesn't want to go back into Henet and you could approach basically Demon levels of intrigue and paranoia.Try not to get noticed by other Mummies, because if they do they may just decide you are wasting your time as a servant of the Judges and try to force you back into the cycle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 09-20-2016, 07:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:08:54-07:00","id":973076,"title":"","content":"All of them. Honestly I think the gamelines work best when you can focus on one splat, maybe including one or two as &quot;NPC only&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T06:58:21-07:00","id":973111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972176#post972176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'ma be blunt: I don't understand this idea that Beast somehow failed in being the crossover game. Some of y'all saying that, unpack it for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I define crossover games as created specifically and exclusively as crossover. In the case of Beast, the rules for other games were not reprinted (I agree with the decision) and I don't think it was stated that when we say vampires we mean kindred and so on. That would be a crossover game. Basically, crossover is not an option but a feature. Beast could be standalone but does lean towards including some other games at a minimum. To suggest to look to Vampire 2e for more info about vampires is not really any different than what every game does. I would not go so far to say Beast failed to be a crossover game. It was as close to being a crossover game as could be made without actually making a crossover game. Honestly tying everything together, makes me wonder how somebody is going to make that Crossover Chronicle work. Even if individual game line rules are left out except as references as they should be, there are probably a hundred groups to relate to each other. It seems a massive endeavor.<br /> <br /> That is the complete opposite of standalone which I assume every game line was designed to be and works equally well in that regard. The themes of a game might lend itself more to standalone. I thought that was more precisely what was originally asked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T07:54:44-07:00","id":973139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=973111#post973111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly tying everything together, makes me wonder how somebody is going to make that Crossover Chronicle work. Even if individual game line rules are left out except as references as they should be, there are probably a hundred groups to relate to each other. It seems a massive endeavor.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's.... quite easy in fact. If I had anything to say about the Crossover Chronicle, I'd outline it in the same way the Eras were written; with only a few gamelines together at a time. Bundle them by theme.<br /> <br /> Hunger: Vampires, Werewolves and Beasts<br /> Espionnage: Demon, Mage and Changelings(not sure)<br /> Humanity: Vampire, Prometheans and Demons<br /> Immortality: Mummy, Vampire, Possessed and Purified<br /> The Nature of Divinity: Mage, Mummy and Demons<br /> Etc...<br /> <br /> And of course you write a chapter or two about how each gameline interlocks with the others, but don't try to write one single cohesive entity with <i>everything</i> in it. That's a doomed endeavour from day 1","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:03:23-07:00","id":973375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/971119-which-cofd-lines-work-best-as-standalone-universes?p=972799#post972799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He means the problem is people run stories where they're dark superheroes because they're missing the point. To be fair many people play Vampire the same way (Dark Sexy Superheroes) (and 1e werewolf basically had it written in). I think when you're ... arrogant ... and know just enough to be dangerous... that often you are not aware of that. I think that many people are playing mage exactly as they'd want to be but because hubris is often blind to the fact, they are too. To be fair superheroes themselves (on that note Dr Strange looks awesome) frequently have victims their hubris (Ultron?), so in some ways perhaps the comparison isn't unfair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without context, that post on Mage looks far more, at face value, as a dismissal of Mage as a CoD setting than anything else. Emphasis on without context. It very likely doesn't mean that but it certainly would not be surprising that it reads like that.<br /> <br /> On Mummy, as addendum to Arcane's comment. Mummy is written very insular, but not as crossover negative. It's a subtle difference, but a difference. I agree though with those that say it's one of the stronger stand alone settings. Also, and this may be me coming from the angle of being a WoD vet but I think people vastly overstate the difficulties of crossover in the CoD. The CoD is massively more conducive to crossover than WoD ever was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 09-20-2016, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T19:46:28-07:00","id":974193,"title":"","content":"Honestly, it might be because my game table has members of 4 splats (Vampire, Hunter, Werewolf and Mage, going on 5 since there's the possibility that the Hunter will become a Sin Eater) that I don't see how one splat could be the &quot;omg, this doesn't work with anything else!&quot;. My players fought Changelings, encountered Ghosts and Spirits, one of them went into the Underworld, they had a meeting with a &quot;God&quot; of Time (Time Spirit of Rank 8) and even went head to head with what they haven't yet identified as an Angel of the God-Machine. Except for Mummies, Beasts and Prometheans they have encountered NPCs of almost all of the Name: the Gerund splats and frankly, there's space in the world for all of those and much more. And it's not detracting from the story, it's adding. It's rewarding when I see the eyes of Vampires and Hunters go wide with &quot;omg, this exists?!&quot; and then the eyes of the Mages and Werewolves go &quot;omg, we've seen weird shit, but THIS actually exists?!?&quot; even after all I've thrown their way. Removing that and making it so each splat gets a separate universe without the whole &quot;supernaturally diverse monster biome (or necrome in the case of Prometheans and Vampires) would be somehow, IMHO, lessening the game. Afterall, the game is called &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot;, not &quot;Separate Universes of Darkness&quot;. Each splat should be a part of the overall Chronicles, not an isolated story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11807,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","user":"HTaiji","date":". 09-21-2016, 10:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T17:06:33-07:00","id":990165,"title":"","content":"Unless I'm building a Beast or Hunter setting I tend to only include one game's content at first. I try to really narrow in on a particular game's themes so I can get the most out of that. That way if I do include crossover content it ends up being a curve ball that nobody was expecting to have to deal with, and it hits that much harder.<br /> <br /> If I'm running Hunter then I downplay the societal world-building for the monsters and focus on small groups and individuals. That way the players can get a really good challenge in, but not get overwhelmed by some sort of coordinated retaliation by a court of faeries or corporation of the damned. I haven't gotten to play or run Beast yet, but when I do I'd like to play up the societal world-building and nudge people to form connections that blur all the boundaries and make a mess of stuff.<br /> <br /> So I guess my answer is 'it depends.'<br /> <br /> The only game I really feel much need to run by itself though is Mummy. I feel like Mummy gets more mileage out of itself by being the main focus. Maybe throw a vampire or two in there as examples of unconventional Lifeless, but not the whole society or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-20T16:06:25-07:00","id":990673,"title":"","content":"Core Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> It works as an interesting game on its own, plenty scary without the themes of Hunter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-23T07:55:10-07:00","id":991851,"title":"","content":"I crossover Mummy, Demon and Mage away from all the others in their own little bubble of contained weirdness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}